WEBVTT

00:07.480 --> 00:09.830
The Animal Soldiers are digging a grave

00:09.830 --> 00:12.220
for Red's body after they dispose of him.

00:13.490 --> 00:15.260
We're not playing with sand here!

00:15.260 --> 00:16.800
Shoo!

00:19.770 --> 00:20.850
Yelling at kids is exhausting.

00:20.850 --> 00:23.160
You okay, Devilcat?

00:23.160 --> 00:23.670
I don't know.

00:35.130 --> 00:38.210
Digging this just by ourselves is taking a while, huh.

00:39.970 --> 00:41.680
What are you doing, Usa?

00:42.700 --> 00:43.660
Kayoko!

00:43.660 --> 00:44.360
Red!

00:45.720 --> 00:47.650
We're digging Red's grave.

00:47.650 --> 00:48.450
You shouldn't do that!

00:48.450 --> 00:51.000
Mud stains don't come off easy, you know.

00:51.000 --> 00:51.700
You do it.

00:51.700 --> 00:54.620
You really expect me to dig my own grave?

02:48.940 --> 02:50.850
You're still here?

02:50.850 --> 02:53.710
I told you last night that I had this morning off, didn't I?

02:54.220 --> 02:56.240
More importantly, take a look at this!

02:57.040 --> 02:58.670
This article over here.

03:02.860 --> 03:06.220
Oh yeah, they <i>did </i> mention something about getting interviewed.

03:06.220 --> 03:07.600
Isn't it amazing?

03:07.600 --> 03:10.260
Those monsters at Vamp's are so well-trained.

03:10.260 --> 03:12.510
Could you imagine a man-eating shark <i>saving </i> a boy?

03:12.510 --> 03:16.520
That's almost like that <i>tsundere </i> thing everyone talks about these days.

03:17.510 --> 03:18.370
What's wrong?

03:18.370 --> 03:22.500
The story here is a bit different from what I've been told, that's all.

03:22.500 --> 03:23.470
This is what they told me:

03:27.130 --> 03:28.440
He saved someone's life?

03:28.440 --> 03:30.030
That's right.

03:30.030 --> 03:32.580
He saved someone from drowning.

03:32.580 --> 03:34.770
Shucks, you're making me blush.

03:34.770 --> 03:36.190
That's quite an accomplishment.

03:36.190 --> 03:38.760
Yes, I'm so proud of him.

03:38.960 --> 03:42.490
We decided to have a picnic near the Tama River that day because of a blackout,

03:42.490 --> 03:42.940
and then...

03:42.940 --> 03:44.100
Are you going to swim?

03:44.100 --> 03:46.110
Time for a dip!

03:46.110 --> 03:48.010
Seeing the river made me want to go for a swim for some reason.

03:48.010 --> 03:49.610
I'm a shark monster, right?

03:49.610 --> 03:51.530
Swimming is like second nature to me, plus I have really scaly skin.

03:51.530 --> 03:53.220
Why does having scaly skin matter at all?

03:53.220 --> 03:56.680
But my senses become dull if I don't jump into water once in a while.

03:56.680 --> 03:57.820
Baths usually do the trick,

03:57.820 --> 04:01.420
but I'd much rather swim in an open area where I can reunite with nature.

04:01.420 --> 04:03.630
Oh yeah, did you know that killer whales living in aquariums have bent fins because—

04:03.630 --> 04:05.910
Get on with the rest of the story already!

04:05.910 --> 04:08.560
So I noticed a lot of noise coming from the riverbed as I was innocently swimming by,

04:08.560 --> 04:09.560
and just when I was starting to wonder what was going on:

04:09.560 --> 04:10.860
Sakaki!

04:10.860 --> 04:12.980
Oh no, the current's flowing too fast!

04:12.980 --> 04:15.560
A child was caught in the river's downstream current!

04:15.560 --> 04:17.740
And so you saved him?

04:17.740 --> 04:18.750
Yes sirree.

04:18.750 --> 04:21.210
His parents were so grateful about it.

04:21.210 --> 04:23.980
After we told them it wasn't a big deal too.

04:25.210 --> 04:26.320
By the way...

04:26.520 --> 04:27.070
Yes?

04:27.370 --> 04:30.470
You guys are supposed to be an <i>evil </i> organization, right?

04:30.670 --> 04:32.640
Yes, what about it?

04:32.640 --> 04:34.500
Never mind.

04:36.960 --> 04:38.200
That means,

04:38.200 --> 04:41.490
this part about him jumping into the river while practicing his killer move

04:41.490 --> 04:43.250
because he suddenly heard a kid screaming must be...

04:43.250 --> 04:44.340
It's all bull.

04:44.340 --> 04:45.400
A big sack of BS.

04:45.400 --> 04:48.250
I guess he was just trying to sound cool then.

04:48.250 --> 04:49.380
Jesus.

04:49.380 --> 04:52.300
I knew they'd try to show off like this.

04:52.300 --> 04:53.830
Well setting vanity aside,

04:53.830 --> 04:56.290
he <i>did </i> save someone's life in the end.

04:56.290 --> 04:58.340
I guess so.

04:58.340 --> 05:00.730
And they call themselves an "evil organization."

05:00.730 --> 05:03.670
"I think anyone would have done the same thing if they were in my shoes."

05:03.670 --> 05:06.600
"I don't think I did anything out of the ordinary," it says!

05:06.600 --> 05:08.360
It <i>was </i> out of the extraordinary, he's a flippin' shark!

05:08.360 --> 05:10.790
I didn't think evil organizations could be so modest.

05:10.790 --> 05:13.030
It even says that he's going to meet the mayor soon.

05:13.030 --> 05:15.390
Isn't that impressive for an evil organization?

05:15.390 --> 05:17.410
What exactly are you trying to say?

05:19.160 --> 05:20.630
Nothing, really.

05:20.630 --> 05:26.310
I might have been thinking that <i>someone else </i> should also be out there saving people's lives too.

05:26.310 --> 05:27.810
I would have...

05:27.810 --> 05:30.070
I would have saved the kid too if I was there.

05:30.070 --> 05:31.620
But you wouldn't find yourself in those situations

05:31.620 --> 05:34.270
if all you ever do is just lounge around at home.

05:40.670 --> 05:45.600
That goddamn CR Edo no Hanayome II...

05:50.450 --> 05:51.550
Oh well.

05:51.550 --> 05:52.990
I guess I'll go get some money from the ATM.

05:55.560 --> 05:58.200
What the hell, the money's not in yet.

05:58.200 --> 05:59.820
Hurry up, you little punk!

06:00.820 --> 06:02.850
That line's going faster now!

06:02.850 --> 06:05.060
Damn it, mom, you forgot to send my allowance!

06:05.060 --> 06:07.180
I'm supposed to be going on a date today too.

06:07.180 --> 06:09.370
Don't you move a muscle!

06:09.370 --> 06:11.330
You better not try anything funny.

06:11.330 --> 06:12.670
Stuff all the money into this bag!

06:15.240 --> 06:16.150
No way.

06:16.350 --> 06:17.710
Hurry it up!

06:18.910 --> 06:19.810
No freakin' way.

06:19.810 --> 06:21.010
A real robbery?

06:21.010 --> 06:23.530
I've never seen one of these before.

06:23.530 --> 06:25.690
You better not be calling the police!

06:25.690 --> 06:29.700
Holy shit, this is just like how they do it on Cops!

06:30.020 --> 06:34.440
Maybe <i>someone else </i> should also be out there saving people's lives too.

06:34.440 --> 06:37.650
Yeah, if I stop the bank robbery:

06:40.890 --> 06:42.990
It'll make even bigger headlines than Vamp's story!

06:42.990 --> 06:44.090
All right!

06:44.090 --> 06:46.880
All of you gather around in one place!

06:47.180 --> 06:49.440
You in the red, get your ass over here!

06:49.440 --> 06:50.370
All righty.

06:50.870 --> 06:52.330
Where's the money?

06:52.330 --> 06:54.030
I-I'll have it soon!

06:54.410 --> 06:56.580
It's still a bit early.

06:56.580 --> 07:00.040
It'll probably be best to get him while he's trying to escape with the money...

07:00.940 --> 07:01.820
Not so fast.

07:01.820 --> 07:03.060
Who the hell are you?

07:03.460 --> 07:06.140
Super Knuckles!

07:06.740 --> 07:08.470
and then I'll tell him:

07:08.470 --> 07:10.870
It may have been a lucky day over at the pachinko arcade,

07:10.870 --> 07:13.540
but it sure was an unlucky day for you.

07:14.540 --> 07:15.600
That was cool!

07:15.600 --> 07:17.070
I'm gonna go with this!

07:17.070 --> 07:17.910
Here's the money.

07:17.910 --> 07:18.880
All right.

07:18.880 --> 07:19.660
You, over there.

07:20.660 --> 07:21.710
M-Me?

07:21.710 --> 07:26.590
I'm sure I won't have to explain what'll happen to this girl if you call the police.

07:27.500 --> 07:29.890
He's got a hostage now!

07:29.890 --> 07:31.650
I guess I can't be so picky anymore.

07:31.650 --> 07:32.380
Hey you!

07:33.180 --> 07:35.910
Let Shiori go!

07:37.530 --> 07:38.830
Kenji!

07:38.830 --> 07:40.410
Don't you even think about it.

07:40.410 --> 07:42.710
If you come any closer, I'll...

07:42.710 --> 07:44.090
Hey, this is serious business!

07:44.090 --> 07:45.310
Leave this to the professional—

07:46.950 --> 07:47.520
You dumbass!

08:00.120 --> 08:02.700
I was so scared, Kenji!

08:02.700 --> 08:04.420
It's all over now, Shiori.

08:04.420 --> 08:05.880
That was quite a feat there.

08:07.220 --> 08:10.430
When I saw that Shiori was in danger I had no choice but to get him with my super tackle.

08:11.430 --> 08:14.150
So you're on the rugby team and Shiori's the team manager?

08:14.150 --> 08:15.320
That's right.

08:15.320 --> 08:21.300
Oh no, no one in school is supposed to find out that we're going out!

08:21.300 --> 08:23.430
Ah crap, I didn't think about that.

08:24.780 --> 08:26.210
Like I said,

08:26.210 --> 08:28.070
that was all thanks to me!

08:28.070 --> 08:30.920
If I didn't flick his knife away at that moment,

08:30.920 --> 08:33.720
that girl might not even be alive right now.

08:33.720 --> 08:35.890
In other words, you missed your chance to shine

08:35.890 --> 08:39.150
all because you were busy trying to think of cool things to say.

08:39.150 --> 08:41.220
Cool things to say, huh?

08:41.220 --> 08:42.660
That wasn't it!

08:42.660 --> 08:45.280
Even Heroes like us

08:45.280 --> 08:47.480
need time to mentally prepare, you know.

08:47.480 --> 08:48.420
Anyway,

08:48.420 --> 08:51.550
things would have been much more dangerous,

08:51.550 --> 08:53.200
if I hadn't knocked his knife away with the pachinko ball.

08:53.200 --> 08:56.270
That's almost as if I saved the girl myself!

08:56.270 --> 08:59.570
Mr. Red's supposed to be a <i>Hero</i>, right?

08:59.570 --> 09:01.190
I really wonder sometimes.

09:01.190 --> 09:04.320
Are you guys even listening to what I'm saying?!

09:15.390 --> 09:17.800
Even a forced smile is a smile.

09:17.800 --> 09:18.630
A smile.

09:18.630 --> 09:20.140
So when the going gets tough,

09:20.140 --> 09:21.440
When the going gets tough.

09:21.440 --> 09:24.440
you don't want to stop smiling.

09:24.440 --> 09:27.150
Can we really do it?

09:30.120 --> 09:31.810
Those are some fine words.

09:31.810 --> 09:33.580
A little pointless since you can't see our faces though.

09:40.730 --> 09:43.680
This shrimp's been fried so perfectly!

09:43.680 --> 09:45.900
I couldn't possibly make this at home.

09:46.480 --> 09:47.790
So you understand it too.

09:47.790 --> 09:49.750
Since the shrimp meat on the inside is slightly rare,

09:49.750 --> 09:51.550
you can taste the juiciness from the cooked meat

09:51.550 --> 09:54.240
and the sweetness from the rare meat coming together as one.

09:54.240 --> 09:55.900
The coating is so crunchy too.

09:55.900 --> 09:59.810
This is no ordinary home cooking, this is the work of an artisan.

09:59.810 --> 10:00.890
You're damn right, it is!

10:01.290 --> 10:05.030
This kind of skill was not perfected in a day.

10:05.030 --> 10:06.940
Kind of like global domination, right?

10:06.940 --> 10:08.290
Exactly!

10:08.290 --> 10:10.500
Every time I eat this tempura,

10:10.500 --> 10:14.710
I am reminded of how important it is to renew my vows daily.

10:14.710 --> 10:16.880
General Vamp and General Hengel.

10:16.880 --> 10:18.520
They may seem very different in terms of character,

10:18.520 --> 10:21.250
but thanks to those differences, they share an excellent relationship with each other.

10:27.490 --> 10:28.500
Once every four years or so,

10:28.500 --> 10:30.120
even Sunred finds himself

10:30.120 --> 10:32.550
unable to suppress his boiling urges.

10:34.140 --> 10:36.230
What are you all groaning about?

10:36.930 --> 10:37.700
What a perv.

10:37.700 --> 10:38.560
As if!

10:40.220 --> 10:42.400
Thank you for calling Florsheim's Kawasaki Division.

10:42.400 --> 10:44.020
It's me, lemme talk to Vamp.

10:45.020 --> 10:46.800
He went to the hot springs on the deluxe coach?

10:46.800 --> 10:48.490
Then I'll go with...

10:48.490 --> 10:49.250
I'll just make do with you.

10:49.250 --> 10:50.710
Call the other monsters right now.

10:50.710 --> 10:51.850
We're gonna fight, man.

10:51.850 --> 10:53.500
One monster won't be enough,

10:53.500 --> 10:55.280
so bring out all your available monsters.

10:55.280 --> 10:57.670
I'll destroy your guys' base if you don't!

10:57.870 --> 10:59.450
Where's my battle suit?

10:59.450 --> 11:02.040
My, my, aren't you in the fighting mood today.

11:07.940 --> 11:09.650
There you are, you monsters!

11:09.650 --> 11:11.480
You won't get off easy, Red!

11:11.480 --> 11:13.650
Today will be your funeral!

11:13.840 --> 11:15.530
We won't lose!

11:15.530 --> 11:16.920
Red, I kill youz!

11:20.120 --> 11:21.760
Forget it.

11:21.760 --> 11:23.010
Stay right there, Red!

11:23.010 --> 11:24.350
You're running away?

11:24.350 --> 11:25.610
Thank goodness.

11:25.610 --> 11:26.550
I kill youz!

11:27.910 --> 11:29.930
Why do I feel this sense of defeat?
